---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-date-range-field</code> is a text field for a start and an end date. Type two dates joined
  by a dash, such as <code>11/3/2026 - 11/9/2026</code>, or open the calendar from the button or
  with Alt + Arrow Down, pick the start, then the end. The calendar shows two months
  (<code>months</code>) and closes once the end is picked.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%; max-width: 320px;'>
    <wc-date-range-field id='date-range-field-demo' label='Trip' value='2026-11-03/2026-11-09'></wc-date-range-field>
  </div>
  <script is:inline>
    const rangeField = document.querySelector('#date-range-field-demo');
    rangeField.addEventListener('input', function (event) {
      myConsole.log('input :: ' + event.detail.value);
    });
    rangeField.addEventListener('change', function (event) {
      myConsole.log('change :: ' + event.detail.value);
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<p>
  The value is two ISO dates joined by a slash: <code>2026-11-03/2026-11-09</code>. Picking the start
  fires <code>input</code> with <code>2026-11-10/</code>; picking the end fires <code>change</code>
  with the whole range. A typed range that ends before it starts is put in order.
</p>

<p>
  <code>wc-date-range-field</code> replaces <code>wc-date-field range</code>, which still works but is
  deprecated and will be removed in 4.0.
</p>
